# The build context is what the Dockerfile copies and nothing else (an allowlist): the
# package, the samples package (samples/), their metadata and the lockfile. Keys (.env),
# data, the evaluation, the docs, the site and the tests stay out, so that a build of a
# checkout never carries a key or a document into an image (tests/test_container.py
# checks the list against the Dockerfile).
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
!samples/
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.pyc
samples/**/__pycache__/
samples/**/*.pyc
